KZ3 patch 2206: Options > Graphics, the page with the Quality preset row. ENHANCEMENT (display; High, the game's own look, is the default).
New libs/video/rsx_gfx_page.h (platform-free, host test tools/smoke/test_display_mode.c): the lever table, the two preset tables, the Custom rule as a pure function
(rsx_gfx_classify: values equal the High table = High, the Ultra table = Ultra, else Custom), the load check of display.ini `quality` against the values, the
multiplayer lock (game type 1..3 answers the High table, saved values untouched), the "kb:gfx <cmd>" bridge commands (quality, bloom, res/aa/sharp, lock, reset) as a
function on a state the host owns, and the page generator rsx_gfx_page_gum (one select per landed lever, Ultra only when a landed lever's Ultra value differs from High;
today only Bloom has landed, so the preset row offers High and Custom). rsx_display_mode.h: rsx_dm_ini_quality, rsx_gfx_quality_name/parse, rsx_dm_ini_write_ext5 (the
quality key beside bloom); the Bloom row leaves the Display page (Options > Display keeps Field of view, Frame rate limit, VSync, ...; RSX_DM_GUM_BLOOM stays as a
no-op flag) and Display's Reset to defaults sends "gfx reset" so Bloom still resets.
Not here: no Ultra lever (render resolution, host anti-aliasing, texture sharpness are declared with ESTIMATE Ultra values and stay off until the host passes their bit),
no motion blur row, FOV and the frame limit stay on Display.

